### Verification trail (seven independent checks, all run 2026-10-24)

1. **OpenRouter — Z.ai catalog** (`https://openrouter.ai/z-ai`): GLM-5.3 entries are `z-ai/glm-5.3`, `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash`, **`z-ai/glm-5.3-flashx`** and `z-ai/glm-5.3-prime` — four separate IDs, each with its own guide page. This is the **only** source that establishes this SKU exists, and it is what makes this a zero-data self-exclusion rather than a phantom one.
2. **models.dev — Zhipu catalog** (`https://models.dev/api/zhipuai.json`): the only two Zhipu entries containing "5.3" are `zhipuai/glm-5.3-flash` (102 providers, 1,000,000 ctx / 131,072 out, open weights, $0.00/$0.00, released 2026-08-26) and `zhipuai/glm-5.3` (114 providers, 1,000,000 / 131,072, open, released 2026-08-14). **No flashx entry under either spelling.** Note the precedent: `zhipuai/glm-4.7-flashx` *does* exist in the same catalog (8 providers), so an X-tier variant is a real pattern for this vendor.
3. **Artificial Analysis:** `/models/glm-5-3-flash-x` → **404**, `/models/glm-5-3-flashx` → **404**, `/models/z-ai-glm-5.3` → **404**. No Intelligence Index, speed, latency or cost-per-task figure exists.
4. **Hugging Face:** `zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash` exists (321B params, MIT, image-text-to-text, fp8, arXiv 2602.15763) with real eval results — **but no `-X` variant repo exists**; `zai-org/GLM-5.3-FlashX` returns 401. Those HF eval results belong to the *Flash* model, not this one, and are deliberately **not** transferred here.
5. **Bing**, both spellings (`"GLM-5.3-Flash-X"` and `"GLM-5.3-FlashX"`): zero relevant hits — only unrelated livescore pages. No benchmarks, no launch post.
6. **Z.ai's blog/docs:** no GLM-5.3-Flash-X announcement or model page found.
7. **Cross-check of the sibling SKUs:** the same seven-source pass confirmed `glm-5.3-flash` is well documented (Intelligence Index 42, #6/121, 68.9 tok/s, TTFT 3.29 s, $0.15/$0.50, 320B total / 18B active, Terminal-Bench 2.1 84.3, DeepSWE 63.4, Agents Last Exam CLI 26.3, ParseBench 70.75) — all of which is *adjacent* evidence recorded in `model/glm-5.3-flash/` by other raters, **not** evidence about the X tier.

### Conflict / resolution notes

- No conflicting sources were found, because only one source carries any data for this SKU and all the others are silent.
- **Identity vs. evidence — the key distinction in this file.** Unlike the nine phantom slugs in this queue, `glm-5.3-flashx` is a **real, separately-routed SKU**: OpenRouter lists it as its own ID with its own guide and parameter set, and the vendor has a documented precedent for an X tier (`glm-4.7-flashx` in models.dev). What is missing is not identity but **every spec and every benchmark**.
- **Explicitly not conflated:** the closest real and well-documented model, GLM-5.3-Flash, is a *different* model — different weights status (open vs this SKU's unverifiable one), different documentation, and a separate folder already researched by other raters. Per `RULES.md` only the ID actually measured may be cited, so none of GLM-5.3-Flash's Terminal-Bench 2.1 84.3, DeepSWE 63.4, Index 42 or $0.15/$0.50 pricing is applied to this folder. The X tier may be a serving profile of the same weights, but no source states that, so it cannot be assumed.
- **Surfaced for the orchestrator, not acted on:** this slug appears in `model-queue.md` with a computed Overall of 81.7 — the **highest-ranked** slug in this entire pass that could not be verified, which is worth noting given how thin its evidence is. Under `RULES.md` a folder is permanent and only a *user* may park a slug. This file therefore makes no parking recommendation and no deletion — it records the negative finding and stops.
- **Re-rate trigger:** if Zhipu publishes a weights repo, a model card, or benchmark figures for the X tier — or if models.dev adds a `glm-5.3-flashx` entry with specs — this file should be superseded by a scored `Step_5_Preview.md`. Until then, no defensible score is available.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Not applicable — self-excluded. No verified specs or benchmarks exist for this SKU, so no quality dimension can be scored without inventing data (`RULES.md` no-hallucination rule; template SELF-EXCLUSION).

